                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0d27c66-4103-32db-8493-762eacbf7a8a",
                        "entry_id": "6d3a5770-29f6-36a7-a2eb-047985ee725b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A road designed for use by trams or wagons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7267302c-da3a-4a0e-95d0-e1d8d3e1e83e",
                                "sense_id": "f0d27c66-4103-32db-8493-762eacbf7a8a",
                                "text": "About two hundred and fifty years ago, some genius, as unknown as the inventor of the lathe, laid the first wooden tramroad, to enable a horse to draw forty-two cwt. instead of seventeen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "791f15dc-e9f0-45fc-b102-bb6e8c7dd6fd",
                                "sense_id": "f0d27c66-4103-32db-8493-762eacbf7a8a",
                                "text": "It is not improbable that, in some locality where tram-roads were a novelty, their name may have been associated in folk-etymology or by pre-scientific etymologers with that of the engineer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99bffd55-f6cf-4727-94f5-84051a8d368f",
                                "sense_id": "f0d27c66-4103-32db-8493-762eacbf7a8a",
                                "text": "Immediately to the west of Coleorton, an important system of tramroads was built in connection with the Ashby-de-la-Zouch Canal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a7cd93e-b3a7-4ffe-81ee-d2fcb0c384e8",
                                "sense_id": "f0d27c66-4103-32db-8493-762eacbf7a8a",
                                "text": "The company arranged for access to a Blackpool terminus […] over a street tramway to be constructed by, and leased for 21 years from, the Corporation. The distance between termini was about eight miles, of which 6 miles 22 ch. was to be tramroad on private right-of-way."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
